  "goodToKnow": "Der Dekan (die Dekanin) is the dean of a university faculty (Fakultät or Fachbereich), elected by the faculty for a few years. The whole university is led by a Präsident or Rektor. Das Dekanat is the dean's office, where students go for admin matters. In the Protestant and Catholic churches, a Dekan oversees a district of parishes. From Latin decanus, a leader of ten. Plural: die Dekane."
